<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Zap (245)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>zap &lt;unit&gt; &lt;dil&gt;@&lt;zone&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>zap Papi send_prompt@update
zap room aggressive@function
</pre>
<p>Removes a DIL program from a unit: the opposite of <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Copy</a>. The 
unit comes first, then the program's name. The unit can be self, room 
(the room you are in), a room anywhere by its symbolic name (room@zone; 
only rooms may be named that way), or someone or something here. Things 
from the treasure zone are refused.
</p><p>You are told "DIL successfully removed." or "Unable to remove the DIL in 
question." See which programs a unit runs with wstat &lt;unit&gt; functions 
(see <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wstat</a>). It is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Copy</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wstat</a>
</pre>




</div>